        "agent": "claude",
        "fact": true,
        "recordText": "Support says several Pro customers were charged twice for their October invoice, and the provider's dashboard shows two successful charges a few seconds apart for each of them. Find the cause and fix it. Run the tests before you finish.\nI found the cause and fixed it. All 8 tests pass, including a new one for this case. **Cause:** `chargeInvoice` in `src/billing.js` generated a new idempotency key on every retry. When the provider charged the card but the response timed out, the retry went out under a different key. The provider treated it as a new charge, so the customer was charged twice a few seconds apart. **Fix:** The key is now generated once per invoice and reused by every retry. If an invoice is re-run after failing, it reuses the key from its first recorded attempt. With the same key, the provider returns the first …",
        "changed": [
          "test/billing.test.js",
          "src/billing.js"
        ],
        "test": {
          "command": "npm test",
          "result": "ℹ pass 8"
        },
        "pass": true
